  "description": "DUDXEG01 crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C248 H168 Ce13 N54 O60 5+,3(Cl1 1-),C1 O3 2-,25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 12 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce10 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce11 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce12 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce13 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 33 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.362-5.177 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 116.55-168.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce13(ccnm)6(CO3)14(H2O)6(phen)18]Cl3(CO3)·25H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
